{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:59:20.631792Z","id":"467f9c1a2c96cd6da6f7fde24f65d0039c61f89d85be2d6e5e8278bebb82350a","body":{"detail":"Only `flutter build macos --debug` was built, with DebugProfile.entitlements (no sandbox, no keychain group). The Release target uses this file with the project's ad hoc identity; macOS requires a provisioning profile for keychain-access-groups, so a Release build may be killed on launch by amfid until it is signed with a team identity. flutter_secure_storage needs the group to store the API key in the sandboxed app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"efa97308a88e35f883cbfe3d5224dea64d0c21a7a94b3b46f973d3c4fe7780c5"},"suggested_fix":"Build and launch the Release app once (V1); if it is refused, sign with a team identity or drop the group for local builds.","summary":"keychain-access-groups is a restricted entitlement: a Release build signed ad hoc (CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY \"-\") may be refused at launch","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:04:07.305024Z","id":"a3db09a4c6e4f331c98204b99bd160a150a5a2dcceddef6b4aa33ae99f2cb2db","body":{"detail":"flutter_secure_storage 11.2.0 (pubspec.lock) defaults MacOsOptions.usesDataProtectionKeychain to true (lib/options/macos_options.dart in the package; flutter_secure_storage_darwin 0.4.3 FlutterSecureStorage.swift:285 then sets kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain). Writes to that keychain need a keychain-access-groups entitlement and a signing team; this file has none and the Debug Runner is signed ad hoc (CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY \"-\" in macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj), so the API key read and write on the macOS Debug build are expected to fail with errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018). Not run: nothing reads or writes the key yet. The Release side of the same entitlement is record 467f9c1a on macos/Runner/Release.entitlements.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"53b6faa8ed2e1b87f1c79671af7fe065933c3b314dc117e5b180590251e91e7e"},"suggested_fix":"Where the SecureKey is built for macOS, pass `MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false)` for builds without the sandbox (the login keychain needs no entitlement), or give Debug a team and the access group; cover it with a write-then-read check on the macOS build.","summary":"flutter_secure_storage on macOS defaults to the data protection keychain, which needs a keychain-access-groups entitlement the Debug build does not have","tags":["review","macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:07:37.346880Z","id":"0345c880fd1f93233280241f94f1507de9f75f4bcc20564533eda1abe1d76ba1","body":{"detail":"xcodebuild: `\"Runner\" has entitlements that require signing with a development certificate. Enable development signing in the Signing & Capabilities editor.` (BUILD FAILED). The same Release build with keychain-access-groups removed from the entitlements succeeds. A Release macOS build needs a team identity, or the group dropped for local builds.","kind":"comment","references":"467f9c1a2c96cd6da6f7fde24f65d0039c61f89d85be2d6e5e8278bebb82350a","summary":"Confirmed at build time: `flutter build macos --release` fails before launch","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:10:56.103042Z","id":"8c37e781745868692b5756ebb69fc591d8b4fc24103233e27f57cfbc998bf2ad","body":{"detail":"`flutter build macos --release` in apps/clax_app: `✓ Built build/macos/Build/Products/Release/clax_app.app (73.6MB)`, exit 0. The Release binary started in the background stayed alive 5 s and exited 143 on SIGTERM to its PID. `codesign -d --entitlements -` on Contents/Resources/clax shows app-sandbox and inherit; on the app, app-sandbox, device.audio-input, network.client and network.server; `codesign --verify --deep --strict` passes. tool/sandbox_probe.dart built as the Release entry point (`flutter build macos --release -t tool/sandbox_probe.dart`) printed: sandbox container dev.empathic.clax, `--version: exit 0, clax 0.4.0`, serve on a free loopback port with CLAX_HOME in the container, `healthz: 200`, `serve exit: 0`, PASS (exit 0). The API key's storage without an access group is on thread a3db09a4.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d9b5c984","summary":"Release.entitlements no longer carries keychain-access-groups; `flutter build macos --release` succeeds and the sandboxed app runs clax","supersedes":"467f9c1a2c96cd6da6f7fde24f65d0039c61f89d85be2d6e5e8278bebb82350a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:10:56.103235Z","id":"49a69b2fc62b928af00869c82f28ebe1737bf9216f539b6a361bd83c5e46ad8e","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements dropped keychain-access-groups (commit d9b5c984), because it is a restricted entitlement that the ad hoc signed Release build cannot carry. The SecureKey implementation (lib/platform/secure_key.dart, FlutterSecureStorage key \"anthropic_api_key\") must construct FlutterSecureStorage with `mOptions: MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false)` so macOS uses the login keychain, which needs no access group, in Debug and Release alike. Spec §3.2 in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md states this.","kind":"comment","references":"a3db09a4c6e4f331c98204b99bd160a150a5a2dcceddef6b4aa33ae99f2cb2db","summary":"Neither macOS entitlements file has a keychain group now: the key store must pass MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false)","tags":["requirement","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:36.587278Z","id":"16d036b29bc1d7c70033d331261896ff553dc779aa486aa80c040a64cd7f56c1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8b8dff15","summary":"The key store builds FlutterSecureStorage with MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false) (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart, FlutterSecureKey.macOsOptions; test/ui/settings_test.dart 'the key store uses the login keychain on macOS' passes). tool/secure_key_probe.dart, which writes, reads back and deletes a probe value with those options under its own storage key, printed 'write ok / read matches / delete ok / PASS' (exit 0) built with flutter build macos --debug (no app-sandbox entitlement) and again with --release (codesign shows app-sandbox).","supersedes":"a3db09a4c6e4f331c98204b99bd160a150a5a2dcceddef6b4aa33ae99f2cb2db","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:39.631392Z","id":"593bc01d88fa804f2f00a83f6c0935e0384799f93672b42ee8e9c2a76f19e563","body":{"detail":"macOS has no ringer switch the app can read, and Focus state is not readable without extra entitlements, so play Tink/Pop at volume 0.6 of the output; a muted output plays nothing. Android (CuesChannel.kt silenced()) skips the tone for silent, vibrate, zero notification volume and Do Not Disturb. The channel lives in MainFlutterWindow.swift rather than its own CuesChannel.swift so that Runner.xcodeproj needs no new file reference.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"0a6b8e9df1d888618e46487852ddfed486f439496592c95b46eaf7674d1e05b5"},"summary":"macOS cues play whatever Focus or mute state the Mac is in, at output volume","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:50:09.005625Z","id":"bc48d382986138a09acf1ed808e40813cad4db7e11b2792811c6cb1c2c56d70d","body":{"detail":"AppDelegate.swift typechecks against FlutterMacOS (xcrun swiftc -typecheck) but the app was not built after the Info.plist UTExportedTypeDeclarations/CFBundleDocumentTypes change. Unverified: Finder opening a .clax in Clax at cold start (the channel is installed in applicationWillFinishLaunching from mainFlutterWindow; a nil controller there would drop the cold-start file into pendingBundles with no channel until the next open), and sandbox read access to the opened path from Dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"9a35917583e696813c7e4806a420a9c8f15732de0637f9775fd33d45822d925e"},"summary":"The macOS document type and application(_:open:) delivery are unbuilt and unexercised","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:31:38.428819Z","id":"b253c18882b350fa28f8a1c732b9db9722dfe1e321020a44e7283c13882dc64b","body":{"detail":"The Bazel-built Clax.app (//apps/clax_app:macos_app at 0c1b42af) launched and made its window, but this session had no permission to send Apple Events to System Events (osascript error -1743) and screencapture -l failed ('could not create image from window'), so Clax > About Clax was never chosen and the panel never captured. target/flutter-app/shots/about-mac-{light,dark}.png were drawn by a scratch program that calls NSApp.orderFrontStandardAboutPanel with the built app's Info.plist name, version, copyright and icon and About.credits over its haiku.json: they show 'Clax', 'Version 1.0.0 (1)', a haiku in grey serif italic and 'Copyright (C) 2026 Empathic, Inc.'. macos_app_test checks the compiled MainMenu.nib names showAbout: and 'About Clax'. Unverified: the menu item reaching AppDelegate.showAbout: through the nib's target, and a new haiku on a second opening while the panel is already up. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §7.4's Option-click on the About haiku for another is not built here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"46d199714ae17efaf22eaf80edb34cce644b538307f5d7537a894ce61fbce84c"},"suggested_fix":"On a Mac with Accessibility allowed for the terminal, open the Bazel-built app with a scratch CLAX_APP_DIR, choose Clax > About Clax twice, and capture the panel with screencapture -l<window ID>.","summary":"About Clax was not opened from the menu of the running app; the About render comes from a harness","tags":["needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/NativeDialogs.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:33:08.474051Z","id":"2b8009b0e2ae8a647077a72961a72bfbebb8e92a328afa020b192d76766335bd","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_dialogs_test checks isHeldReturn on synthesized events and that the default button is disabled until the injected schedule fires, and a scratch AppKit harness running AlertRun as a sheet confirmed the view tree (Allow disabled before arming and enabled after, 'Always allow' after the suppression button is clicked, dismissAlert answering the cancel index). Not verified: that the local keyDown monitor swallows a held Return on a real key sheet, that a fresh Return after arming presses the default (the harness process could not become active, so the sheet never took keys), and how the sheet looks (screencapture -l has no screen-recording permission from an agent shell; cacheDisplay and dataWithPDF of the sheet render blank). The capability prompt from the kit example's net call has not been seen in the built Clax.app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":290},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"a4ba05afc89b21685c6fc65ea92e634c62cb9c2e90b68eaeb22cdf85041350d6"},"suggested_fix":"Drive the built app (scratch CLAX_HOME) to a capability prompt and capture the window before and after arming, as the macOS chrome test does for its states; press and hold Return across the arming.","summary":"The armed alert's keys and its pixels are unverified in a running app","tags":["verification","macos","native-overlays","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/NativeDialogs.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:33:08.475488Z","id":"1d5f6e83889cc39b85110c21dea16ce2bc8c5f4a8f30ede18924d8fd5166b76f","body":{"detail":"NSMenuItem.subtitle is macOS 14.4+; on macOS 12–14.3 the detail (such as the model name of a choice in Settings, lib/ui/settings_screen.dart:744) is dropped from the native menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"217163049e979ac06320c791bd7ee194a8a173346366db037aad9a5a593cae09"},"suggested_fix":"Before 14.4, append the detail to an attributedTitle in secondaryLabelColor.","summary":"A menu item's detail shows only on macOS 14.4 and later","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/EditBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:12:10.832702Z","id":"f7f77ff562d5807e069ba6faef726e58db3e57f0548453e768bef4c03020f4fb","body":{"detail":"Checked: the compiled nib item by item (tool/macos-app-check.sh, macos_app_test), the Dart side over mock channels (test/ui/app_menu_test.dart, test/ui/shortcuts_test.dart), and that the built Clax.app launches and shows its window with MenuBridge and EditBridge installed. Not checked: that AppKit sends ⌘C, ⌘V, ⌘Z to EditBridge while a Flutter TextField has the focus rather than Flutter's own shortcuts taking them first (either way the field gets them); that flutterHasFocus sees a WKWebView first responder as a page (the walk up superviews); that Edit's items validate through NSApp.target(forAction:) for a page; that the claxMenuAction: key equivalents (⌘K, ⌘[, ⇧⌘H) fire while a page has the focus. screencapture and System Events were not permitted in the session that built it, so no menu-*.png exists. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.8 asks for an integration test of ⌘C and ⌘V in a page field and in a Flutter field; none exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"69ad5b01e8a6ed8a8280e1090513f7d220ce5961495b6b523c6353f7d8b04964"},"suggested_fix":"Add the integration test (integration_test/, dev.empathic.clax/test-input can be extended to send key events) and capture each menu into target/flutter-app/shots/menu-*.png.","summary":"The native menu bar and both bridges are unverified in a running app: no menu was opened, no key equivalent pressed, no ⌘C/⌘V tried in a page or a Flutter field","tags":["needs-verification","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:12:10.832747Z","id":"cc237a21cecaff1161b00ce64927e5cefda2b544a24e4ff2f2e23b7873c8641b","body":{"detail":"The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.8) says Clax Help opens the docs but names no URL, and nothing in the repository names a documentation site; the GitHub path follows the release URL in the README (github.com/empathic/clax).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"d3f805871ee1bf0349e80fed35bf72656dd639647cf65a2a0ca3b52d1be6cf3e"},"summary":"Help › Clax Help opens https://github.com/empathic/clax/tree/main/docs, a guess at where Clax's documentation lives","tags":["status:needs-decision","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
